{"seq":11,"trial_id":"v03-pilot-2026-10/hermes-haiku-gbrain-verbs-told-mu-v03-dev/sy-02-marrow-agrisupply-sites/r2","wall_ts":"2026-10-29T19:19:03.036Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"69a2a2aa09959f5bbcca551effc37e8ddea13305ea6e5b01940a91666ec4bae3","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV03PIL0001","text":"Pree, I found two sites for Marrow Agrisupply in #central-team, both from the June 9, 2026 escalation thread:\n\n1. **Eastbank**: Hollis is handling the setup. Ticket PD-4821 has the Eastbank receiving-door import attached, but the file labels doors E1/E2 while the booking sheet uses 01/02. Someone needs to reconcile those before reimporting, or duplicates get created.\n2. **Pine Crossing**: Your morning receiver says the appointment screen shows only the afternoon shift. A driver who arrived at 7:10 had his trailer number written on a sticky note. Hollis is checking the shift template and asking support to reproduce it with the store login.\n\nThe thread also refers to other stores, but without names. Three rows in Marrow's rollout tracker say only \"waiting,\" and you were going to get names and blockers from store ops. Hollis wanted that list by noon. None of that list is in the channel, so I can't add those stores.\n\nI left out two possible matches. The Wichita store dispatcher appears in a 2025 #central-team message, but that message doesn't tie him to Marrow. The Salina North yard in the January 2026 Central handoffs digest belongs to a different account (Marrow Fieldworks / Pree's dealer account), not Agrisupply.\n\nSources: the #central-team history and the June 9 messages in it. I didn't search other channels. The gbrain search returned the same June 9 thread plus unrelated notes, and the public Central files don't list any Marrow Agrisupply sites."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV03PIL0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
